{{short description|Theme from the film The Good, the Bad and the Ugly}}
{{use mdy dates|date=February 2026}}
"'''The Good, the Bad and the Ugly'''" is a theme composed by [[Ennio Morricone]]. It first appeared in the 1966 [[The Good, the Bad and the Ugly|film of the same name]], and was included on the [[The Good, the Bad and the Ugly (soundtrack)|film soundtrack]] as "The Good, the Bad and the Ugly (main title)", with [[Bruno Nicolai]] conducting the orchestra. A [[cover version]] by [[Hugo Montenegro]] in 1967 was a pop hit in both the US and the UK.<ref name="Hyatt">Hyatt, Wesley (1999). ''The Billboard Book of #1 Adult Contemporary Hits'' (Billboard Publications), p. 66.</ref> It has since become one of the most iconic scores in film history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.udiscovermusic.com/stories/the-50-best-film-scores-of-all-time/|title=The 50 Greatest Film Scores of All Time: 3. ''The Good, the Bad and the Ugly'' (1966)|date=July 12, 2025|author=[[Jason Zumwalt]]|website=uDiscoverMusic|access-date=February 1, 2026}}</ref>

